    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0677" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2844a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ramer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-02T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Referring to Department’s 41, December 9, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d485-f1"/> Department has requested Navy Department to order that
                    proposed investigation along Honduranean frontier be made at once. It is
                    especially desired that officer should visit Somoto because of reports regarding
                    unneutral activities of commandante there.</p>
                <p>When officer starts inform American Legation Tegucigalpa in order that facilities
                    for his return through Honduras may be extended.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
